# The recovered archives are BYTE ARTIFACTS, not text. Git's autocrlf stripped 18,435 CR bytes
# from april-aof-raw.aof on its first commit (2,808,112 -> 2,789,677) and would have canonized
# an unparseable file that still looked correct in a directory listing -- RESP delimits on
# \r\n, so removing CR destroys the format the archive IS.
#
# Marking them binary is not a preference. It is the difference between an archive and a story
# about one.
*.aof   binary
*.rdb   binary
